      "translatedText": "None means no robust loss is added, and the constraint error is treated as its square\\. HuberLoss and CauchyLoss are used to reduce the influence of constraints with large errors; they cannot guarantee the removal of all incorrect matches, and they also affect constraints with large errors that are actually valid\\.",
